[[2047,31,0,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>The supply for the speedometer \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               (pin 10 of connector\nA) is controlled by the ignition (INT) by the line for fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B11</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               up\nto 2/99 or fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F4</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of the additional fuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98B</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               from\n2/99.</p><p>Similarly, the rev counter \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E15</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               (at\npin 15 of connector A) and the centre instrument \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               (pin\n1.).</p><p>An earth signal from instrument light dimmer\ncontrol \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               reaches pin 6 of connector B of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              . This\nalso receives a side light activated signal, at pin 5 of connector\nB (\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <a href=\"#/3233770\">E2010</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ).</p><p>According to the logic processed by the\ninternal electronic device, the speedometer \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               sends the\nlighting signal to the other instruments: to the centre instrument \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               (pin\n7) from pin 12 of connector A;  and to the rev counter \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E15</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               (3\nof connector B) from pin 4 of connector B.</p><p>Switch \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               symbols are lit up when\nthe side lights are switched on through the line coming from the\nswitch for the steering column switch unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H5</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p>"]]